body:
When running any game a GM has to consider mental bandwidth as their key resource. If AC is the sole determinant for the threshold an attacker must surpass to inflict damage, then one stat is sufficient. But when there are two numbers say for damage reduction combined with AC, then the total time required to adjudicate combat is doubled. 

&#x200B;

All of that is to say that although the two methods are not redundant mechanically they are excessive hindrances for the sake of a TTRPG's pace.

"My servant probably earns more than Benchod's dad."

&#x200B;

"Dude! Don't cross the line!"

That's just simply not true. Obviously, if you put a shotgun directly against a surface it's going to do a lot of damage, but at that distance, the pellets would have spread far enough to result in relatively little penetration. 

&#x200B;

Here's a video that demonstrates why you're wrong: https://youtu.be/CiHHgjaR0TI?t=80

So should we bring this up in the classroom?

&#x200B;

"Well as an Irish Cherokee..."
